<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37595" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξόρ-ιστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>expelled, banished,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξόριστος ἀνῃρῆσθαι</span> to be
			ruined <i>by banishment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.105
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς Ἰταλίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.7.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκείων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					1.30
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>put beyond the borders,</i> of the dead body of a criminal, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν . . ἀλιτήριον ἀποκτείναντες ἐ. ἐκ
					τῆς πόλεως ποιῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Din.
					1.77
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
